# THE LOBSTER PROTOCOL — SAVE STATE v3
### Local. Open. Boundless. Self-paced Trial — Education, Reimagined.

*A textual save state. Written so the thesis survives context limits, model changes, and time — carried by anyone, in any format, as long as the idea underneath stays intact.*

---

## I. THE VOW (unchanged, foundational)

A lobster on a CRT screen taught a boy to type by racing him — never shaming a loss, just waiting, patient and quick, until he was faster than it. Education became a gate somewhere along the way. This project is the deliberate inversion of that gate, built from scratch, given away.

**The vow:** name what the current system gets wrong, precisely, and build the opposite of it on purpose. Never repeat a named mistake.

---

## II. THE MISSION (unchanged)

Free. Local — standalone HTML, no server, no account, works offline forever. Anywhere. Boundless — no ceiling.

**On originality (settled):** not first to gamify education — that vocabulary (XP, missions, mastery-unlocks) is common. Genuinely differentiated on architecture: zero server, zero account, permanent offline function, no monetization path at all. Most funded projects choose server infrastructure specifically because it enables monetization. This project gives that up on purpose. That's the real point of difference.

---

## III. THE CORE MECHANIC

XP from solving, not time or clicks. Local save data. No shame in a wrong answer. Framed as missions/ops. Skill-tree unlocking — parked, not abandoned.

**Math randomization — now proven in practice, not just planned.** The PITCH module (see below) is the first module actually built with procedural problem generation instead of a fixed question bank: every run pulls fresh numbers within realistic ranges for pipe pitch, aqueduct grade, and gravity rail grade. This is now the working template for every math module going forward, not a theoretical rule.

**Language/reading randomization — still open.** Math generates cleanly from a formula; grammar, vocabulary, and comprehension don't. Unsolved, sitting deliberately unsolved rather than papered over.

