## X. THE INVERSION LEDGER

| Old System | LOBSTER |
|---|---|
| Age-locked pacing | Mastery-locked pacing |
| Punitive failure, shame | Retry-with-consequence-shown, forward-only XP |
| Compliance over curiosity | Interest-driven unlocking (skill tree, long-term) |
| Gatekept by geography and income | Free, local, downloadable, no account |
| Abstract before concrete | Real-world grounding, always — named explicitly per concept |
| One assumed learning style | Multiple senses — visuals, generated sound, game-feel |
| Fixed question banks | Procedural randomization (math proven, language open) |
| Minimum-compliance teaching | Teaching the reasoning behind the standard, not just the number |
| Test without a teacher | Tutor page + quiz, linked, not two separate things |

---

## XI. STATUS AT THIS SAVE STATE

Five modules built. Two process documents exist alongside them. The tutor-then-quiz structure and procedural math randomization are both proven in working code, not just described. The "teach toward genuine competence" principle got refined mid-conversation — worth keeping the correction, not just the original version, since the corrected version is the truer one.

**Still open:** skill tree shape, language/reading randomization, translation pipeline, first-aid module format, module naming/indexing convention at scale.

**Load-bearing, unchanged:** free, local, no accounts, mastery over calendar, no shame in failure, mute always available, no binary-only theming for younger tiers, no copying — only inversion and remix, collaboration not solo creation.

